hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27680","Haddathana Sufyan: Haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, from Siba' ibn Thabit: I heard from Umm Kurz al-Ka'biyyah, who narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Hudaybiyyah, and I went seeking meat: For the boy two sheep, and for the girl one sheep; it does not harm you whether males or females. She said: And I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Leave the birds upon their roosts."
"27681","Haddathana Sufyan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, from Siba' ibn Thabit, he said: I heard the people of Jahiliyyah circumambulating while saying: Today we cool the eye; we strike the two Marwahs."
"27682","Haddathana Sufyan, from Ubayd Allah, from his father, from Siba' ibn Thabit, from Umm Kurz al-Ka'biyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, and Sufyan once said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prophethood has gone, and there remain the bearers of glad tidings."
"27683","Haddathana Sufyan, from Amr, from Ata', from Habibah bint Maysarah, from Umm Kurz al-Ka'biyyah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: For the boy two equal sheep, and for the girl one sheep. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father saying: Sufyan errs in these hadiths; Ubayd Allah heard them from Siba' ibn Thabit."
"27684","Haddathana Affan, he said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Zayd, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, he said: Siba' ibn Thabit narrated to me from Umm Kurz that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said concerning the aqeeqah: For the boy two like sheep, and for the girl one sheep."
